{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/124031","id":4691949267,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABF6l20w","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124031","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124031.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124031.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124031","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/124031/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/124031/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124031/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/ea764bfc9989beb81e3d692eaa547852ff2ea377","number":124031,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Stabilize directional shadows cascade radius so they don't jitter in XR","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Fixes https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/73402\r\n\r\nIt turns out the issue with directional shadows jittering in VR was \"accidentally\" improved considerably by https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116424\r\n\r\nWith the changes from that PR (already merged in `master`), if the `XRCamera3D` is close to the world origin, there will be no shadow jittering! However, moving even 20 units away from the world origin will bring back some jittering, and the further away you move, the worse it becomes.\r\n\r\nAs explained in [this comment](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/73402#issuecomment-5896921299), I discovered that \"stabilizing\" the data from OpenXR (ie keeping the previous values unless the change was over a certain threshold) would almost entirely eliminate the jitter.\r\n\r\nHowever, this problem is visible in WebXR too, and presumably all other XR interfaces, so this PR attempts to propagate the same stabilization up into the renderer to where it has an effect on directional shadows. Rendering isn't my strongest area, so I'd love some feedback from the rendering folks on if this could cause any unexpected issues elsewhere.\r\n\r\nBut, with this PR, the shadow jittering in VR is almost entirely eliminated in my testing. I've tested with OpenXR on Meta Quest 3 as well as PCVR (Linux streamed to the Meta Quest via wivrn), and with WebXR","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098111,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgxMTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:rendering","name":"topic:rendering","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":865585000,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw4NjU1ODUwMDA=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:xr","name":"topic:xr","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":nul